# build output
dist/
# scratch build outputs (e.g. `astro build --outDir dist-c1`); real builds use dist/
dist-*/
# generated Astro types
.astro/
# deps
node_modules/
# tsconfig.json is a real, required config file but is caught by the repo-root
# `.gitignore` `*.json` rule; re-include it here.
!tsconfig.json
# CI clone target for resolve_sources.py --clone
sources/
# env / logs
.env
.env.production
*.log
# macOS
.DS_Store

# Phase C1 — API cross-reference inventory.
# The MERGED lookup is regenerated (by scripts/build_inventory.mjs and by the
# xref integration at astro:config:setup); it is already covered by the root
# `*.json` rule and must NOT be committed. Listed here for clarity:
src/generated/xref-inventory.json
# Per-version inventories that Phase C2 drops here ARE the committed source of
# truth, but the root `.gitignore` ignores all `*.json` — re-include them:
!.api-inventory/*.json
# (emitters/*/_out is already ignored by emitters/*/.gitignore.)

# Phase C2 — generated, regenerable API content.
#   * Per-version API trees (api/dev/**, api/0.35/**, ...) are large and fully
#     regenerable by scripts/build_versions.py, so we ignore every directory one
#     level under api/. The evergreen `api/index.mdx` and the (regenerable but
#     committed) `api/compatibility.mdx` are FILES, not matched by `*/`, so they
#     stay tracked.
src/content/docs/api/*/
#   * versions.json is regenerated by build_versions.py (scans the api/<V> trees
#     that exist). Ignored; code falls back to a committed-safe default
#     (src/lib/versions.ts DEFAULT_MANIFEST, astro.config readLatestVersion).
src/generated/versions.json
